# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Both the site and the brain read it.

# ── Browser (the site) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A dev agent in cortex mode, and a publishable key whose allowed origins include
# http://localhost:4321. Without these the site falls back to the simulated voice.
PUBLIC_AGENT_ID=
PUBLIC_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Brain (../local.py) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent's secret sk_ key, from create_agent_credentials (it switches the agent
# to cortex mode). Never commit it.
VOQALIZE_AGENT_SECRET=
# Optional: defaults to the dev relay.
# VOQALIZE_CORTEX_URL=wss://cortex.dev.voqalize.com/agent
# GEMINI_API_KEY is read from your shell if it is not set here.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Analytics (PostHog, docs/analytics.md) ────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: the site and the brain default to the Voqalize Marketing Website project.
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Defaults to https://t.voqalize.com (the managed reverse proxy); https://us.i.posthog.com goes direct.
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
# Source maps (pnpm build:release): a personal API key with error tracking write + organization read.
# POSTHOG_CLI_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_CLI_PROJECT_ID=658890

# ── Optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where /api is proxied in dev (default https://app.dev.voqalize.com).
# VOQALIZE_API_TARGET=
# Load an unreleased avatar runtime instead of the published one.
# AVATAR_RUNTIME=https://avatar.dev.voqalize.com/runtime/current.js
